/*
Problem: Count Equal and Divisible Pairs in an Array (LC 2176)
Topic: Array / Brute Force

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Check every possible pair (i, j).

A pair is valid if:

1. nums[i] == nums[j]

2. (i × j) is divisible by k

Count all such pairs.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Initialize count = 0.

2. Traverse all pairs where:

   i < j

3. For every pair:

   • Check if the values are equal.

   • Check if:

     (i × j) % k == 0

4. If both conditions are true,
   increment the count.

5. Return the count.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

nums = [3,1,2,2,2,1,3]

k = 2

Valid pairs:

(0,6)

(2,3)

(2,4)

(3,4)

(1,5)

Answer:

5

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

nums = [1,2,3,4]

k = 1

No equal elements.

Answer:

0

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The nested loops examine every unique
pair exactly once.

Each pair is counted only if it
satisfies both conditions.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n²)

Every pair is checked once.

Space : O(1)

Only the counter is used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Brute Force / Pair Enumeration
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int countPairs(vector<int>& nums, int k) {

        int count = 0;

        // Check every pair
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            for (int j = i + 1; j < nums.size(); j++) {

                if (nums[i] == nums[j] &&
                    (i * j) % k == 0) {

                    count++;
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
};
